Rule {Number} ({Description})\n{Rule Definition}
Ex) Rule 21 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
    {v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0

[Example Rules]
Rule 15 (broadcasting compatibility for tensor shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) − 1 else ndim(v_2) − 1] : ndim(v_1) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1)

Rule 29 (list of floats for weights must match length of a tensor dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(float)} |= v_2.len = shape(v_1, 0) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0

Rule 19 (compatibility of integer or float (data) type tensor and variable)
{v1 : tensor, v2 : int ⊎ float} |= if 1 ≤ dtype(v1) ∧ dtype(v1) ≤ 5 then 1 ≤ v2 ∧ v2 ≤ 5 else if 6 ≤ dtype(v1) ∧ dtype(v1) ≤ 8 then 1 ≤ v2 ∧ v2 ≤ 8 else false

Rule 16 (shape alignment for matrix multiplication)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − 2)) ∨ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − 1) = shape(v_2, 0))

Rule 22 (valid step size for a range)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float, v_3 : int ⊎ float} |= if v_1 > 0 then v_2 ≤ v_3 else if v_1 < 0 then v_2 ≥ v_3 else true

